This repository is the **inter.face** design pipeline. When asked to design or
redesign an interface — web, mobile, tablet, or desktop — run it:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` (the resident router) and `PRINCIPLES.md` (sixteen rules,
   three of them hard: accessibility, keyboard completeness on tool-shaped
   surfaces, human gates).
2. Settle the surface class first — page-shaped or tool-shaped, `TRANSLATE.md`
   row 1, no safe default.
3. Run `loops/01-direction.md` to **Gate A** (the human picks the concept), then
   `loops/02-craft.md` to **Gate B** (the human approves or cuts the technique
   set).
4. Deliver `DIRECTION.md`, `tokens.json`, one design image per surface, and one
   measured prototype per technique. It stops before code.
5. Never publish past a gate without a human decision.
